---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navigation from '../../components/Navigation.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Battery Management System Firmware | Jaspartap Goomer"
  description="Firmware development for the Analog Devices LTC6813-1 BMS for Ontario Tech Racing's Formula SAE electric car. Cell monitoring, balancing, and safety features."
>
  <Navigation />
  
  <main class="max-w-[1100px] mx-auto px-6 sm:px-10 py-16">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <a href="/#projects" class="text-sm text-[var(--accent)] hover:underline mb-4 inline-block">
        ← Back to Projects
      </a>
      
      <div class="mono text-xs tracking-widest text-[var(--accent)] mb-2">CASE STUDY · FIG. 01</div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">
        Battery Management System Firmware
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl opacity-90 mb-6">
        Ontario Tech Racing · Formula SAE Electric Car
      </p>
      
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        {["C/C++", "LTC6813-1", "isoSPI", "SPI", "CAN", "pytest", "HIL"].map(tag => (
          <span class="mono text-xs border border-[rgba(255,255,255,0.5)] px-3 py-1.5">
            {tag}
          </span>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
    
    <!-- Hero Video/Image -->
    <div class="mb-12 rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-[var(--border)]">
      <video 
        autoplay 
        muted 
        loop 
        playsinline
        poster="/bms-loop-poster_7f81.jpg"
        class="w-full"
      >
        <source src="/bms-loop_7208.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
        Your browser does not support the video tag.
      </video>
    </div>
    
    <!-- Overview -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 mono">
        <span class="text-[var(--accent)]">$ </span>Overview
      </h2>
      
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
          For Ontario Tech Racing's Formula SAE electric car, I developed firmware for the Analog Devices LTC6813-1 
          battery management system. This critical safety system monitors and protects the high-voltage battery pack 
          that powers the vehicle.
        </p>
        
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed opacity-90">
          The BMS continuously monitors cell voltages and temperatures across the pack, performs passive cell balancing 
          to maintain pack health, and implements comprehensive fault detection and error handling to ensure driver safety 
          and component protection.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    
    <!-- Challenge -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 mono">
        <span class="text-[var(--accent)]">$ </span>The Challenge
      </h2>
      
      <div class="bg-[var(--card-bg)] border border-[var(--border)] rounded-lg p-8">
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Formula SAE electric vehicles use high-voltage battery packs (up to 600V) that require precise monitoring and 
          protection. Any cell voltage imbalance, temperature excursion, or communication fault could damage the pack or 
          create a safety hazard.
        </p>
        
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed opacity-90">
          The firmware needed to reliably communicate with the LTC6813-1 chip over isoSPI (a galvanically isolated SPI 
          variant), process measurement data in real-time, make safety-critical decisions, and report telemetry over the 
          vehicle's CAN bus—all while meeting Formula SAE's strict safety requirements.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    
    <!-- Solution -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 mono">
        <span class="text-[var(--accent)]">$ </span>Implementation
      </h2>
      
      <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-4">Cell Monitoring</h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed opacity-90">
            Implemented continuous voltage and temperature acquisition for all cells in the pack. The microcontroller 
            communicates with the LTC6813-1 via SPI through an isoSPI transceiver, which provides galvanic isolation 
            between the high-voltage pack and low-voltage control systems.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-4">Passive Cell Balancing</h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed opacity-90">
            Developed algorithms to identify cell voltage imbalances and command the LTC6813-1's built-in discharge 
            resistors to balance cells. This maintains pack capacity and extends battery life.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-4">Fault Detection & Safety</h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed opacity-90">
            Built comprehensive error handling for overvoltage, undervoltage, overtemperature, and communication faults. 
            The system triggers appropriate responses including warnings, derating, or emergency shutdown depending on 
            fault severity.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-4">CAN Telemetry</h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed opacity-90">
            Packaged cell voltages, temperatures, state of charge, and fault status into CAN messages for the vehicle's 
            ECU, dashboard, and telemetry system. Used custom Database CAN (DBC) files to define message structures.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-4">Testing & Validation</h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed opacity-90">
            Verified firmware behavior through pytest-based Software-in-the-Loop (SIL) tests that simulated various 
            operating conditions and faults. Conducted Hardware-in-the-Loop (HIL) testing on bench setups with the 
            actual LTC6813-1 hardware before integration onto the vehicle.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    
    <!-- Gallery -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 mono">
        <span class="text-[var(--accent)]">$ </span>Hardware
      </h2>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="border border-[var(--border)] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
          <img 
            src="/bms4_8e2d.jpg" 
            alt="BMS board mounted on battery pack showing LTC6813 chip and circuitry"
            class="w-full h-64 object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="p-4 bg-[var(--card-bg)]">
            <p class="text-sm opacity-90">BMS board installed on the battery pack</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="border border-[var(--border)] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
          <img 
            src="/bms2_dae8.jpg" 
            alt="Close-up of BMS board showing isoSPI transceiver components"
            class="w-full h-64 object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="p-4 bg-[var(--card-bg)]">
            <p class="text-sm opacity-90">Detail view of isoSPI transceiver and voltage measurement circuit</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="border border-[var(--border)] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
          <img 
            src="/bms3_3e09.jpg" 
            alt="BMS board detail showing passive cell balancing circuitry"
            class="w-full h-64 object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="p-4 bg-[var(--card-bg)]">
            <p class="text-sm opacity-90">Passive balancing circuitry and thermal management</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="border border-[var(--border)] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
          <img 
            src="/bms1_6bb6.jpg" 
            alt="Full view of BMS board on battery pack"
            class="w-full h-64 object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="p-4 bg-[var(--card-bg)]">
            <p class="text-sm opacity-90">Complete BMS installation on the high-voltage pack</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    
    <!-- Results -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 mono">
        <span class="text-[var(--accent)]">$ </span>Results
      </h2>
      
      <div class="bg-[var(--card-bg)] border border-[var(--border)] rounded-lg p-8">
        <ul class="space-y-4">
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="text-[var(--accent)] text-2xl">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="block mb-1">Safety-Critical Operation</strong>
              <p class="opacity-90">
                Successfully monitors and protects the high-voltage pack in all operating conditions, meeting Formula 
                SAE safety requirements.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="text-[var(--accent)] text-2xl">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="block mb-1">Reliable Communication</strong>
              <p class="opacity-90">
                Achieved robust isoSPI communication with zero dropped messages during testing and competition operation.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="text-[var(--accent)] text-2xl">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="block mb-1">Comprehensive Testing</strong>
              <p class="opacity-90">
                Validated through SIL and HIL testing before vehicle integration, catching multiple edge cases that 
                could have caused issues in competition.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="text-[var(--accent)] text-2xl">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="block mb-1">Real-Time Telemetry</strong>
              <p class="opacity-90">
                Provides detailed pack health data to the ECU and dashboard for driver awareness and post-run analysis.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
    
    <!-- Back link -->
    <div class="text-center pt-8 border-t border-[var(--border)]">
      <a href="/#projects" class="inline-block text-lg text-[var(--accent)] hover:underline">
        ← Back to All Projects
      </a>
    </div>
  </main>
  
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    video {
      animation: none;
    }
    video[autoplay] {
      autoplay: false;
    }
  }
</style>
